            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you regarding your patient, a 46-year-old male admitted on 27/06/2020 with confirmed SARS-CoV-2 infection (COVID-19). Diagnosis was established via PCR testing of nasopharyngeal swab. Chest imaging confirmed bilateral pneumonic infiltrates consistent with COVID-19 pneumonia. During hospitalisation, the patient required supplemental oxygen therapy and was treated with dexamethasone and empirical antibiotic cover. Remdesivir was initiated given disease severity. Supportive measures including fluid management and thromboprophylaxis with low-molecular-weight heparin were maintained throughout. The patient showed gradual clinical improvement with resolution of fever and reducing oxygen requirements. He was discharged on 08/07/2020 in recovering condition. Please monitor oxygen saturation, arrange follow-up chest X-ray in 6 weeks, and ensure continued thromboprophylaxis for a further 10 days. Please do not hesitate to contact me should you require further information.</div>"
            },
